//IWAD LORE DUMP TIEM
[enu default]

//The Original Episodes
E1TEXT =	"Well that was a pear-shaped pile of doodoo feces. Good thing this\n"
			"isn't the only episode you get, otherwise you'd be rightfully\n"
			"looking for the nearest big box outlet to get a refund with.\n"
			"\n"
			"Judging from the awful smell and slimy entrails all around you,\n"
			"you must be in Hell's Beach Cabanas. Given the locals there aren't\n"
			"going to be too keen on your presence, looks like the only way out\n"
			"of this terrible vacation spot is straight through; I wouldn't even\n"
			"try for the private hotel rooms if I were you.\n"
			"\n"
			"At least they've got some killer drinks, though. Silver lining.";
/*	Hell's Cabana drinks are killer both figuratively AND literally: Quench your
	tastebuds, fill your belly, mulch your insides, vomit blood for weeks, and
	get posessed by a lost soul, becoming a twisted husk of yourself hellbent on 
	world domination with just a single bottle of Hellfire Guava Fruit Bat 
	Fruit Punch!

	...on second thought, maybe just mix Um Bongo with vodka instead. */

E2TEXT =	"Having dealt with the smug bovine insiting you stay for the blatant\n"
			"tourist trap that was Hell's Shores, you find yourself in the most\n"
			"awful part of hell yet: The Administrative Offices, a horrible place\n"
			"where souls of the damned do mountains upon mountains of paperwork.\n"
			"\n"
			"\nOr worse... retail. Looks like you've gotta take this quest over\n"
			"to their side now, if that wasn't obvious already. You've already\n"
			"dealt with the worst part anyhow... but the red-clad masses of hooves\n"
			"and flying meatball population will try their damnest to prove their\n"
			"laughable counterpoint anyhow. You've got this, buddy.";
/*	Some food for thought: Marble, guts, and hellfire is to the demons as
	cubicles, dingy wallpaper, and quarterly stock reports are to us. Maybe 
	that's the real horror of The Backrooms(tm): How infamously DULL the 
	cubicle job is. */

E3TEXT =	"Like most administrators (and commanders of hellish forces), the\n"
			"biggest one on top's almost always the one that falls the easiest.\n"
			"Just as you're about to finally leave this smouldering heap of\n"
			"brimstone, paperwork, and burning flesh and hitch the nearest\n"
			"teleporter network back to Earth, your comm-device flickers back to\n"
			"life and starts ringing like crazy. ...and it's from Long Dennis,\n"
			"requesting you clean out the demon infestation in his pie factory\n"
			"in the middle of either one of Mars's Moons or Hell itself."
			"\n"
			"With artistic liberty, your angry swearing somehow gets interpreted\n"
			"as a yes, and you get dumped somewhere unfamiliar before you can\n"
			"finish your sentence. Looks like your work isn't done quite yet.\n"
			"\n"
			"In the meantime, you hope Earth's doing okay...";
/*	The reason Dis is as pathetic as it is was that the demons got sick and 
	tired of hearing her bark commands at them, locked her in her admin 
	office... and left her for dead. There's a reason the Plasma Rifle was 
	just sitting around. */

E4TEXT =	"Long Dennis had better appreicate this, not that you had much of a\n"
			"choice in the matter, anyways. Frankly, pot pie factories aren't\n"
			"usually supposed to have the stench of sulfur, screams of the damned,"
			"brimstone, or a lack of any pie crust facilites anywhere in the area.\n"
			"Long Dennis says the hanged corpses are normal though, as those were\n"
			"apparently the Space United Kingdom IRS trying to tax him.\n"
			"\n"
			"And to make matters worse, the big plods murdered your rabbit-human\n"
			"kemono-hybrid son, Jimmy Bunny! He may have been about as bright as\n"
			"a room covered in Vantablack paint, but he was still your pride\n"
			"and joy. That's just a shitty thing to do, demons, very unfunny.\n"
			"\n"
			"Thankfully, you should be en route to Earth by now, and hopefully\n"
			"Little Jimmy can give as much blessing as his brain can allow to\n"
			"give you the support needed to get the demons out.";
/*	Little did Weponguy know that that was FAR from the only pie factory Long
	Dennis had. If he'd been forced to fully clear out all 7,432 of his infested
	pot pie and pot pie accessory factories, Earth would've been gone around #452. */

//Super SIGIL-io Bros.
E5TEXT =	"You're gonna have some rather nasty words to say to Long Dennis\n"
			"once you make it back to Earth. It was already bad enough to have\n"
			"to clear his pie factory, but now his personal offshore hellfire\n"
			"beach cabana? The one back in episode two was already enough of a\n"
			"workout, you don't need this extra crap in your workload...\n"
			"\n"
			"Provided you don't get dumped somewhere unfamiliar again, you've got\n"
			"a job on Earth to do now, and those demons ain't going to murder\n"
			"themselves... not without something to kickstart that, anyways.\n"
			"\n"
			"Lock, load, rip, tear, glory kill, whatever 2016 got started,\n"
			"and what Eternal entered into the mainstream, do all that as well.";
/*	Long Dennis and his people are infamous for their inability to understand
	the concept of "Dude, I've got more important shit to do, maybe later." */

E6TEXT =	"Dang, a sequel to SIGIL exists at all? Count me impressed. Aside\n"
			"that, you're REALLY going to have some VERY choice words with\n"
			"Long Dennis once you finally get back. Once was already bad enough,\n"
			"twice was just plain ridiculous, and now this!?\n"
			"\n"
			"Not cool, Long Dennis, not cool. At least you can finally get\n"
			"to Earth proper, and finally show Satan MacDonald a piece of your"
			"mind. I know I would, but my personal opinion doesn't really matter\n"
			"with these things, especially concerning the quasi-canon.\n"
			"\n"
			"Insert Doom: The Dark Ages reference here.";
/*	The bowels of hell are rich in their time-honored tradition of doors that
	close on your face 30 seconds after you enter the level, and rooms full of
	FIREBLU that hold nothing but measly health/armor bonus pickups.

	You wouldn't get it, it's a cultural thing. */

//The one most people use
C1TEXT =	"Having finally made it to the infested starport, for lack of a\n"
			"better term, your comm device starts blaring out armym'n stuff\n"
			"towards your general direction. Looks like the jerks squatting\n"
			"in your home planet also decided that Earth would make a lovely\n"
			"place for their terrible metal bands as well. (And I mean the\n"
			"awful, overly squealy, detuned as hell kind.) Get as deep as you\n"
			"can into their main studio, slap the big 'ol power switch up ahead,\n"
			"and you'll have saved Earth from having to hear lousy metal music.\n"
			"\n"
			"And actually save their lives too, that might be more important.\n"
			"Anyways, expect a bunch of lard and spiders this level.";
/*	Hell doesn't actually like metal music, they only pretend to as a excuse to
	harass human neighbors, and generally be unpleasant douchebads. 
	Truly distasteful. */

C2TEXT =	"Looks like that power switch you just slapped did more than just\n"
			"cut power to cheap-o, power-guzzling loudspeakers. A big 'ol\n"
			"spaceship takes off into the sky, towards somewhere else in the\n"
			"solar system. Your armym'n voice coming from the comm device says\n"
			"its Earth's evacuation ship. (Wasn't a lot to evacuate, it seems.)\n"
			"\n"
			"...what now? Another ring from you comm deice, and your next goals\n"
			"are clear: Take out that bootleg liquor industry Hell cobbled up\n"
			"somewhere in your hometown. Not wanting to be subject to terrible,\n"
			"watered-down liquor, you get back up, and you get back at it.";
//Space Ireland and Space Scotland both agree that demons make VERY crappy booze.

C3TEXT =	"Would you look at that, seems like awful, bootleg booze wasn't the\n"
			"only thing in that plant~ An awful, fleshy portal that can only be\n"
			"described with 'take our word for it' manifests before you.\n"
			"\n"
			"You've already done most of the legwork to get here in the first\n"
			"place, so don't you dare turn back now! Besides, Space Ireland's\n"
			"got some really, REALLY good liquor in it for you if you manage\n"
			"to save the planet.";
/*	Hell's original plan WAS to just oversaurate the human market with watered-down,
	blood-infested crappy booze, but their military commanders got ornery, and
	that's how the invasion of Earth came to be... or more accurately,
	crudely taped on. */

C4TEXT =	"With Satan MacDonald finally breating his last, his entrails make a\n"
			"prompt and quick trip into Hell's lower orbit, as demons around you\n"
			"instantly kick the bucket left and right. You's did it! You saved\n"
			"The Earth! And you didn't even have to contend with Long Dennis this\n"
			"time! ...you then nervously eye your dwindling stash of NRG-Brew\n"
			"you've been holding on you ever since you got here. When you get\n"
			"home... there's gonna be a LOT of repopulation to do. That's when\n"
			"the REAL challenge begins. Hope you're ready for it, buddy.";
/*	Dutchess is quite notorious for insisting that her husband can go at least 
	15 more hours. */

C5TEXT =	"A left turn instead of a right in the map you were just in might've\n"
			"been a better idea. But no time to kick yourself in the head just\n"
			"yet, you've (presumably) got more jerks, a special kind of jerk,\n"
			"and many MANY orthogonal angles to deal with.\n"
			"\n"
			"Best get movin'.";
/*	Bugs Bunny actually ended up in Wolfenstein 3D once, but considering that
	Warner Brothers were most likely more focused on that superhero reboot of
	Looney Tunes at the time (or was it the 2000s?), his exploits with the Spear
	of Destiny became the lost media. Truly a tragedy of humanity... */

C6TEXT =	"I don't have anything (allegedly) clever to give you here.\n"
			"GLHF, don't die, and don't let the Cyber get you on the way out.";
/*	It wasn't actually the Mastermind that brought the demons to Earth, it was 
	Mortimer McMire. He was REALLY salty after his defeat, and decided the best
	way to deal with a problem is with Scorched Earth policy.*/

//Doom 2: Chain Elementals and Paingunners Edition!
P1TEXT =	"Unsurprisingly, the exit linedef that had flesh growing all over it\n"
			"and the screaming souls of the damned turned out to be Hell's trap.\n"
			"Through the arcane, bullcrap power of cutscene incompetence, you\n"
			"wind up in Demon Jail. Thankfully for you and your mission, whoever\n"
			"was supposed to keep you locked up thought lardtubs and the spiders\n"
			"stashed somewhere in the attic make for good security guards.\n"
			"\n"
			"Now go forth and kill, the WAD ain't gonna get any easier from here.";
/*	It's a terribly hidden secret that demons make lousy watchguards. 
	Blame the sin of Sloth. */

P2TEXT =	"Clearing out that nest of archviles released secrets you've been\n"
			"fearing ever since you got here: Satan MacDonald's half brother's\n"
			"trying to pick up where Maccy last left off, and worse...\n"
			"\n"
			"He's one of those extremely obnoxious livestreamers! Tier Three subs\n"
			"and everything! Your dedication to saving Earth oughta pick up from\n"
			"here if it hasn't; It's only gonna get worse if you let the demons"
			"dawdle to their own devices.";
/* This isn't the only half-brother Satan MacDonald has... but he's the only one
	of the unholy bunch he can tolerate for more than two seconds. Or minutes. */

P3TEXT =	"The stench of dodgy ring lights and cheap-o stage materials fill\n"
			"your nostrils as you enter Hell proper. MacDonald's half-brother's\n"
			"on the ropes now! All you's gotta do is deal with his livestreaming\n"
			"staff, make your way over to his flesh-infested luxury bedroom, and\n"
			"do what you did to Satan MacDonald! Those rockets ain't gonna do\n"
			"their job for you, after all!";
/*	While Hell has its own version of Twitter|X, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube
	and what-have-you, it's a well-known fact that Hell's version of TikTok and
	Bluesky and our TikTok and Bluesky are one and the same. */

P4TEXT =	"Flood lights, ring lights, and all sorts of dodgy streaming equipment\n"
			"violently shatter around you, as do the demons and other jerks running\n"
			"them in the first place. Looks like Earth's safe once again!\n\n"
			"This does mean Hell will have to go back to filming sleazy porno,\n"
			"but at least they're only exploiting their own kind now, rather than\n"
			"dragging humanity down with them in the process.\n\n"
			"Now if you're not mistaken, Dutchess has missed you VERY dearly...\n"
			"and you're still not quite done with the task of repopulating Earth.\n"
			"Hope you packed some heavy coffee with you, this is gonna be a long,\n"
			"long month.";
/*	Weponguy would soon become world-renowned for having brought the once
	endangered bnuuy kemonos back to thriving populations in only about 
	half a year. And for his infamous inability to pull out of a driveway. ;) */

P5TEXT =	"Unfortunately, you fell for one of the oldest tricks in the book,\n"
			"Snide, obnoxious demon cacking blares through your ears as you're\n"
			"dumped in a large, nasty demonic arena. And this one has more than\n"
			"a few of his Cybderdemon pets in it. It's not that they betrayed him,\n"
			"more that they paid beyond the Tier 3 subscription for this.\n"
			"\n"
			"You'd better clear this joint and get the hell out of here, before\n"
			"this mod gets into more detail about that.\n";
/*	The Cyberdemons are the only ones who can afford the subscription anyways.
	Not because the demons don't have money, more that Hell's payment services
	refuse to do buisiness with most demons for dumb, arbitrary reasons, but dump
	what they're doing to handle the purchases of their demonic masters instantly. */

P6TEXT =	"You know what usually happens when you beat MAP31 in Plutonia wads,\n"
			"right? It seems that MacDonald's half-brother had something even\n"
			"worse planned out for you. Normally, you'd have to break out the\n"
			"stockpile of quicksaves and autosaves... but with your improved\n"
			"(so to speak) arsenal, this shouldn't be too bad!\n"
			"\n"
			"Remember to stay calm, keep the pressure going, avoid Cyberdemon\n"
			"solicitation, and remember: The crown jewels are the most common\n"
			"weakness of your average demon. Including the female ones.\n";
/*	It's hard to tell the difference between a male and a female demon... 
	because all of them are ugly. And they're evil too, so I don't think that
	really matters in the long run. */


//MtPain27: The IWAD
T1TEXT =	"Having cleared out the last little bit of problems over at the\n"
			"technological complex, you breathe a little easier, now that Space\n"
			"Ireland (and maybe even Space Scotland) don't have to worry about\n"
			"their fancy brewing equipment going kerput.\n\n"
			"As fun as it would be to reminisce about the wild keg parties you had\n"
			"in the places you roam... you quickly push it aside and march over\n"
			"to their security guard complex.\n\n"
			"Besides, there's a reason Dutchess didn't want you drinking in the\n"
			"first place: Most of the corpses you've seen littered around the\n"
			"place weren't actually due to the demons; People do really, REALLY\n"
			"stupid things when they're drunk.";
/*	Actually, the real reason is that bunnygirls can't stand the smell of most
	boozes, save for sake (rice wine). Do remember, bunnies have very sensitive
	noses, which before their anthro-ization, was to keep track of who's who. */

T2TEXT =	"Earth's external security forces are operational once again!\n"
			"Unfortunately, that was all just the easy part of the mission.\n"
			"Hell's starting to crank out demons like nobody's buisiness now,\n"
			"and it must have something to do with that ugly looking machinery\n"
			"way out in the distnace, almost looking like it's orbiting the\n"
			"planet itself.\n\n"
			"Do what you always do, and make Space Ireland/Scotland proud.";
//I don't have anything clever to put here.

T3TEXT =	"You unfortunately knew you'd have to be going back to Hell to bring\n"
			"the fight to them once again, but looking at a signpost in the\n"
			"distance... oh god no. No no no no no. Not this shit again.\n\n"
			"\"You have Entered Long Dennis's Pot Pie Factory #5,482!\"\n\n"
			"You didn't like having to run this guy's errands the first time\n"
			"around, but actually needing to go there to resolve the main problem\n"
			"is a major punch to the gut. Not only is it cranking out new demons\n"
			"at a horrifying rate, but it's also a well-known fact that demonic\n"
			"pot pies taste HORRIBLE.\n\n"
			"You're gonna have a LOT of choice words to say to Long Dennis if\n"
			"you come out of this alive.";
/*	Long Dennis is a very, VERY gullible sucker, and the demons were able to take
	over the entire place for the cost of fifty euros, a set of novelty plastic
	cups, and some sponge cake in the shape of yellow cake uranium. */

T4TEXT =	"And thus, the jerkwipe that was mulling around in Long Dennis's\n"
			"overly engineered pie factory is now no more. Whilst you'd love to\n"
			"do the same thing to the pie factory itself, on account of the crap\n"
			"you had to deal with in Thy Flesh consumed, it ain't like Dennis\n"
			"himself did much to piss you off. That, and arson's usually illegal.\n"
			"But, overall, you'd have to rate your saving of the entire planet,\n"
			"as well as making your wife happy again, as...\n\n"
			"GRADE: B+, DIFFICULTY: B";

/*	In this timeline, the Deliquent of Doom never came to be, as his entire
	family became the unfortunate (to them) example of what happens when you
	fall into a pot pie meat processing machine. */

T5TEXT =	"...where on earth could you be!? ...wait. Uh oh. You know now.\n"
			"This must be your ex-wife's many, MANY temples, the one you're\n"
			"in presumably a shrine to Anubis. But you know well that no matter\n"
			"whoever god gets worshipped... there sure as hell ain't one in the\n"
			"pantheon in support of being an unfaithful wife.\n"
			"\n"
			"No matter HOW large her tits are.\n\n"
			"A heart of gold is what truly matters when it comes to the ladies,\n"
			"and she can't change that.\n";
//Say it with me now: Celebrity Marriages NEVER last.

T6TEXT =	"Another wrong turn at Ejipt Albuquerque lands you right in the\n"
			"middle of a cruise ticket agency. Before you can even get a single\n"
			"word in, the people running the place decided that you won a free\n"
			"luxury cruise, and sheperded you onto a luxury cruiser ship\n"
			"alongside the most expensive, highest-tier tickers one could get.\n\n"
			"You'd rather not let Space Ireland down, but this could be a good\n"
			"time as any to actually get a break for once. Unfortunately for you,\n"
			"this noble theory gets proven wrong almost immediately by the\n"
			"obnoxious screenching of demons, the rowdy tramping and stompng\n"
			"of cyberdemons, and most likely a whole slew of other demonic\n"
			"problems stopping you from actually taking a vacation.\n\n\n"
			"Friggin' tourists.";
/*	At least he got the GOOD tickets; The Economy Class ticketholders were, in
	actuality, immediately dumped into the ocean as soon as they got on the boat.
	This also happens if you're Jon Arbuckle. */

//Does anyone actually play No Rest For the Living?
NERVETEXT =	"Cyberdemon Billy Bob Joe McJoeseph thought he could turn the Earth\n"
			"into his personal OpenRCT2 session, but you thankfully not only\n"
			"proved him wrong, you've also saved Earth's own rollercoasters too!\n"
			"\n"
			"Rest well, 'ol hero, for until you have to waltz into a space coffin\n"
			"and wake up someteen years later to do it all over again, albiet\n"
			"with fancier graphics, more defined story, and some redesigned \n"
			"demonic jerks... Dutchess will always be waiting for you.\n"
			"\n"
			"No, seriously. Don't keep her waiting. You've still got a lot of\n"
			"repopulating to do, not to mention an awful lot of parenting.";
//Thankfully for everyone involved, the OpenRCT2 developers were proved innocent.